// reducer_b1.cdz — the first REAL Cadenza agent-harness reducer (bootstrap program B1), ML surface.
//
// The §21c end-to-end bar: a Cadenza-authored reducer (NOT the interim Rust wit-bindgen fixture in
// ../reducer-guest) compiled by rcdzc -> wasm-component and driven through the kernel's
// ComponentReducer::apply. Proves the real-Cadenza-reducer path works with the operator's option-C
// boundary (design/agent-harness-kernel.md: reducer.wit stays STRUCTURAL; the kernel host marshals each
// WIT field <-> the shared value-heap runtime's handles around this reducer's handle-ABI apply).
//
// Fold shape — B2 binary-AST value-form boundary (design-binary-ast-abi): the guest apply keeps its
// STRUCTURED args (rcdzc's B3 wrapper value-decodes the event record into them), and RETURNS the flat
// PROTOCOL effect-request record directly — so value-encode(result) IS the kernel wire, no transform:
//   apply(ct: Record{family, version}, payload: Option(Bytes), resumes: Option(Bytes))
//       -> List(Record{ correlation: Option(Bytes), kind: String, payload: Option(Bytes), target: Bytes })
// The effect-request is a FLAT record (no Mk wrapper, no EffectKind sum): `kind` is the lowercased effect
// FAMILY string ("http"/"shell"/any userspace handler family — register-by-string, seq366, NOT a closed
// enum); `target` is Bytes. Fields sorted-key (the shared protocol descriptor the kernel's ast_marshal +
// rcdzc both bake). This is ruling (Q): the guest authors the protocol shape, value-encode is a pure
// structural encode (no Mk-strip / enum->string / string->bytes adapter — no-adapter directive).
//
// B1 BEHAVIOR: a TOTAL fold that IGNORES its inputs and requests NO effects — returns the empty list
// for EVERY event (can't-brick). The minimal fold that proves the path; B2 emits a real effect.
//
// BUILD: cdz compile reducer_b1.cdz --target wasm --component-name cadenza:agent-kernel/fold
//   -> apply emitted as the byte-boundary fold (B3: value-decode event / value-encode result). VALID.
// The cdz-kernel e2e loads this via REDUCER_CADENZA_COMPONENT (nix packages.reducer-cadenza builds it).

// The protocol effect-request is an INLINE flat record (kind a family String, target Bytes, sorted fields)
// — NOT a named-type alias: `type X = Record(..)` in Cadenza is a single-variant SUM (needs match to read),
// but the wire is a bare transparent record, so we spell the record type inline on apply's return.
def apply(
  ct: Record(family: String, version: UInt(32)),
  payload: Option(Bytes),
  resumes: Option(Bytes),
) -> List(Record(correlation: Option(Bytes), kind: String, payload: Option(Bytes), target: Bytes)) = []

// Behavioral coverage (runs on the seed compiler via `cdz test`, INDEPENDENT of the kernel host adapter;
// a plain `cdz compile` ignores @test, so the emitted component is unchanged). Passes = returns unit,
// fails = traps. Guards the B1 invariant: the fold requests NO effects for any event.
@test
def b1_returns_no_effects_for_a_message() =
  if List.len(apply({ family = "message", version = 1 }, None(), None())) == 0
  then unit
  else trap("B1 must return an empty effect list for a message event")

@test
def b1_returns_no_effects_for_a_resume() =
  if List.len(apply({ family = "result", version = 1 }, None(), Some(String.to-bytes("tok")))) == 0
  then unit
  else trap("B1 must return an empty effect list for a resume event")

export { apply }
